      "common:shortName": [],
      "common:generalComment": [
        {
          "#text": "Refractory bricks are materials capable of maintaining structural and performance stability under high-temperature conditions. They are commonly used as linings in high-temperature industrial equipment such as kilns, furnaces, and boilers. Made primarily from high-alumina, silica, or magnesia-based materials, refractory bricks are manufactured through high-temperature firing. They are characterized by high heat resistance, thermal shock resistance, and strong chemical stability, making them widely used in industries such as metallurgy, construction materials, and chemicals.",
          "@xml:lang": "en"
        },
        {
          "#text": "耐火砖是一种能够在高温环境下保持结构和性能稳定的材料，通常用于高温工业设备如窑炉、熔炉和锅炉内衬。其主要原材料包括高铝矿物、硅质材料和镁质材料，通过高温烧制而成。耐火砖具有高耐热性、抗热震性以及较强的化学稳定性，在冶金、建材、化工等行业中广泛应用。",
          "@xml:lang": "zh"
        }
      ],
